cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use comparePlots in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "comparePlots: Compare the Distributions of Variables in jamovi"
version: 1.1.1
date-released: 2026-11-26
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24401092
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/heelgueta/comparePlots"
url: "https://github.com/heelgueta/comparePlots"
abstract: >-
  comparePlots is a jamovi module for comparing the distributions of several
  variables on one shared scale. Numeric variables: box, violin, means with
  error bars, raincloud, ridgeline, histogram, density, ECDF, data points and
  barcode plots, also across the groups of a grouping variable (two groups, with plots made for two groups, or three or more). Ordinal and nominal
  variables: stacked and diverging bars, heatmap, waffle, pictogram,
  parliament, response profile, pie, donut, grouped bars and lollipop plots.
